  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Why create lags?\n",
    "\n",
    "A lag uses information from an earlier week to predict a later week. For example, `cases_lag_1` is the previous week's case count. This prevents the model from using the target week's own case count to predict itself.\n",
    "\n",
    "The lag-correlation checks showed that recent malaria burden carried much stronger predictive information than the weather variables. The same-week previous-year count was also examined separately because using a simple 52-row shift would be unsafe when a year contains 53 epidemiological weeks.\n"
   ]
  },
