  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The seasonal plots suggested broad recurring periods of higher burden, but peak timing shifted between years. That is why seasonality was represented as a smooth cyclic feature rather than assuming that one exact week is always the annual peak.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Time-based train/test split and persistence baseline\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 66,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(260, 31)\n",
      "(104, 31)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "train = model_data[model_data[\"year\"] <= 2022].copy()\n",
    "test = model_data[model_data[\"year\"] >= 2023].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(train.shape)\n",
    "print(test.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 67,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test[\"baseline_prediction\"] = test[\"cases_lag_1\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 68,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Baseline MAE: 32.97115384615385\n",
      "Baseline RMSE: 41.69520817330673\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "mae_baseline = mean_absolute_error(\n",
    "    test[\"cases\"],\n",
    "    test[\"baseline_prediction\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "rmse_baseline = np.sqrt(\n",
    "    mean_squared_error(\n",
    "        test[\"cases\"],\n",
    "        test[\"baseline_prediction\"]\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Baseline MAE:\", mae_baseline)\n",
    "print(\"Baseline RMSE:\", rmse_baseline)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "A **persistence baseline** predicts that next week's burden will simply equal last week's burden. A forecasting model should improve on this simple rule; otherwise, its additional complexity is not providing much value.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Encode annual seasonality with sine and cosine\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 69,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model_data[\"sin_week\"] = np.sin(\n",
    "    2 * np.pi * model_data[\"epidermiological week\"] / 52\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_data[\"cos_week\"] = np.cos(\n",
    "    2 * np.pi * model_data[\"epidermiological week\"] / 52\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 70,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train = model_data[model_data[\"year\"] <= 2022].copy()\n",
    "test = model_data[model_data[\"year\"] >= 2023].copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Weeks are cyclical: Week 52 is close to Week 1 even though their ordinary numerical values are far apart. Sine and cosine map week-of-year onto a circle so the model can represent that continuity. Both are needed because together they describe position around the annual cycle without creating an artificial break between the end and beginning of the year.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Negative Binomial Model 1: recent case lags + seasonality\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 71,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(256, 33)\n",
      "(104, 33)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "features_model1 = [\n",
    "    \"cases_lag_1\",\n",
    "    \"cases_lag_2\",\n",
    "    \"cases_lag_3\",\n",
    "    \"cases_lag_4\",\n",
    "    \"sin_week\",\n",
    "    \"cos_week\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "train_m1 = train.dropna(\n",
    "    subset=features_model1 + [\"cases\"]\n",
    ").copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "test_m1 = test.dropna(\n",
    "    subset=features_model1 + [\"cases\"]\n",
    ").copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(train_m1.shape)\n",
    "print(test_m1.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### A modelling problem we encountered: convergence\n",
    "\n",
    "The first unscaled Negative Binomial attempt produced a convergence warning. That failed fit is not rerun in this cleaned notebook. The practical fix was to standardize the four case-lag predictors using statistics learned from the training data only, then refit with the L-BFGS optimizer and more iterations.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an example of a numerical estimation problem rather than evidence that Negative Binomial regression itself was inappropriate.\n"
   ]
  },
