   "source": [
    "A high-burden week was defined using the 75th percentile of the 2018-2021 development period (206.25 cases, effectively 207 or more because case counts are integers).\n",
    "\n",
    "The balanced logistic classifier looked promising on 2022 validation but generalized poorly to 2023-2024: it detected only half of the truly high-burden weeks and produced many false alarms. The classifier is therefore retained as an exploratory experiment, not as a dependable operational warning system.\n"
   ]
